# Surakkha web — environment variables (development).
#
# The web app talks to the api over HTTP only; the api → simulator
# control channel is invisible to the SPA. The web app does NOT need
# `SIMULATOR_SECRET` — that secret is shared between the api and the
# simulator processes only.
#
# The SPA always fetches `/api/*` (same-origin). The dev server's
# Vite proxy (configured in `vite.config.ts`) forwards `/api/*` and
# `/auth/*` to `http://localhost:3000`. In production, the reverse
# proxy / orchestration layer is responsible for routing `/api/*`
# to the api container.
#
# There is no `VITE_API_BASE_URL` knob — the apiOrigin is wired in
# `main.tsx:122` as the literal "/api" by design (same-origin proxy
# is the only supported deployment model in v1).
